window.docContents[81].resolve({"/Colorings/#section-making-greedy-efficient":{"contents":"Our definition of greedy has allowed us to prove the greedy colouring bound, but\nhow good is greedy as an algorithm? As promised, we now investigate why\nevaluating it on dense graphs is slow, and what to do about this. If you have no\ninterest in efficient algorithms or debugging, skip to\nComputing Colourings of Encodable Graphs: all it needs from this\nsection is that, by the end of it, #eval runs a faster implementation of greedy.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","context":"Graph Theory in Lean\u0009Colorings\u0009Greedy Colouring*","header":"7.8.6. Making  greedy  Efficient*","id":"/Colorings/#section-making-greedy-efficient"}});